{'query': 'reputable peer-reviewed scientific source on causes and effects of climate change', 'results': [{'title': 'Causes and Effects of Climate Change | United Nations', 'url': 'https://www.un.org/en/climatechange/science/causes-effects-climate-change', 'snippet': 'This leads to global warming and climate change. The world is now warming faster than at any point in recorded history. Warmer temperatures over time are changing weather patterns and disrupting the usual balance of nature.'}, {'title': 'Causes of Climate Change | US EPA', 'url': 'https://www.epa.gov/climatechange-science/causes-climate-change', 'snippet': 'Causes of Climate Change. Natural processes are always influencing the earth’s climate and can explain climate changes prior to the Industrial Revolution in the 1700s.'}, {'title': 'Climate Change - NASA Science', 'url': 'https://science.nasa.gov/climate-change/', 'snippet': 'What are the effects of climate change? The effects of human-caused global warming are happening now, are irreversible for people alive today, and will worsen as long as humans add greenhouse gases to the atmosphere.'}, {'title': 'What are the effects of global warming? | National Geographic', 'url': 'https://www.nationalgeographic.com/environment/article/global-warming-effects', 'snippet': 'Global warming and climate change are often used interchangeably as synonyms, but scientists prefer to use “climate change” when describing the complex shifts now affecting our planet’s weather and climate systems.'}, {'title': 'What evidence exists that Earth is warming and... | NOAA Climate.gov', 'url': 'https://www.climate.gov/news-features/climate-qa/what-evidence-exists-earth-warming-and-humans-are-main-cause', 'snippet': 'There is overwhelming scientific evidence that Earth is warming and a preponderance of scientific evidence that human activities are the main cause.'}], 'result_count': 5, 'duration_seconds': 5.0561919000174385}
{'query': 'government or international body report on causes and effects of climate change', 'results': [{'title': 'Climate Change | United Nations', 'url': 'https://www.un.org/en/global-issues/climate-change', 'snippet': 'Climate change refers to long-term shifts in temperatures and weather patterns. Although some climate variations occur naturally, human activities have been the main driver of climate change since the 1800s, mainly through the burning of fossil fuels such as coal, oil, and gas.'}, {'title': 'Causes of Climate Change | US EPA', 'url': 'https://www.epa.gov/climatechange-science/causes-climate-change', 'snippet': 'Burning fossil fuels changes the climate more than any other human activity.Causes of Climate Change. Natural processes are always influencing the earth’s climate and can explain climate changes prior to the Industrial Revolution in the 1700s.'}, {'title': 'NASA is a global leader in studying Earth’s changing climate.', 'url': 'https://science.nasa.gov/climate-change/', 'snippet': 'What are the effects of climate change? The effects of human-caused global warming are happening now, are irreversible for people alive today, and will worsen as long as humans add greenhouse gases to the atmosphere.'}, {'title': 'Climate change', 'url': 'https://www.who.int/health-topics/climate-change', 'snippet': 'Between 2030 and 2050, climate change is expected to cause approximately 250 000 additional deaths per year from malnutrition, malaria, diarrhoea and heat stress alone. The direct damage costs to health are estimated to be between US$ 2–4 billion per year by 2030.'}, {'title': 'Climate change - Greenpeace UK', 'url': 'https://www.greenpeace.org.uk/challenges/climate-change/', 'snippet': 'Climate change, or global warming, is causing extreme weather and sea level rise, putting hundreds of millions of people’s lives at risk. But it also presents an opportunity to change the way we live for the better.The causes and effects of climate change.'}], 'result_count': 5, 'duration_seconds': 9.77191949999542}
{'query': 'global average temperatures trend 2023 2024 latest data', 'results': [{'title': 'Climate change: global temperature | NOAA Climate.gov', 'url': 'https://www.climate.gov/news-features/understanding-climate/climate-change-global-temperature', 'snippet': 'Yearly surface temperature from 1880–2024 compared to the 20th-century average (1901-2000). Blue bars indicate cooler-than-average years; red bars show warmer-than-average years. NOAA Climate.gov graph, based on data from the National Centers for Environmental Information.'}, {'title': 'Global Temperature - Earth Indicator - NASA Science', 'url': 'https://science.nasa.gov/earth/explore/earth-indicators/global-temperature/', 'snippet': 'Global temperatures in 2025 were cooler than 2024, with average temperatures of 2.14 degrees Fahrenheit (1.19 degrees Celsius) above the 1951 to 1980 average. The data shown are the latest available, updated annually.'}, {'title': 'Climate Pulse - Near real-time updates of global climate variables', 'url': 'https://pulse.climate.copernicus.eu/', 'snippet': 'Surface air temperature anomaly. Baseline: 1991-2020 Data: ERA5. Credit: C3S/ECMWF. Climate Pulse provides near real-time updates of key global climate variables from the Copernicus Climate Change Service (C3S).'}, {'title': 'Bringing the big data of climate change and the conversation into...', 'url': 'https://climateclock.net/', 'snippet': 'Using the past 5 years of data, we calculated the rate of change of annual emissions. We assume fossil fuel CO2 emissions follow this trend, while additional CO2 emissions from deforestation remain constant at the average level of the past 5 years.'}, {'title': 'Global warming | Definition, Causes, Effects, Solutions... | Britannica', 'url': 'https://www.britannica.com/science/global-warming', 'snippet': 'Global warming, the phenomenon of increasing average air temperatures near Earth’s surface over the past one to two centuries, happens mostly in the troposphere, the lowest level of the atmosphere, which extends from Earth’s surface up to a height of 6–11 miles.'}], 'result_count': 5, 'duration_seconds': 5.636971900006756}
